+# Character editor reflow
+
+The user requests continued meticulous visual improvements and useful features within plan usage and system headroom. The current production Change look editor has a zero-height character at320x568/390x664 with200% root text, and hidden right-edge controls at640x360/default text and enlarged landscape/desktop. An offline native baseline probe captured10 layouts; subsequent acceptance tests reproduce6 failing layouts while5 cases pass, including draft name/caret preservation across resize.
+
+Keep the existing form, draft model, choice groups, finite preview owner and save/cancel behavior. Correct shrink constraints on the stage/name field so the options stay inside their panel. Use the existing named app-shell container and normal page scrolling for cramped text; retain a160px character drawing area, let the title occupy a complete line beneath Cancel/Save, and let the options grow. Reflow narrow species choices to readable horizontal rows, face choices to two columns, swatches to fitting columns and tabs to balanced rows. Preserve normal fitted layouts when their contents fit. Add8px scroll margin for native focus outlines. No new React state, listener, timer, frame owner or persistence change.
+
+Verify10 viewport/text combinations:320x568,390x664,640x360,844x390,1280x800 at100%/200% root text. Check every initial visible control has a44px target, complete horizontal bounds and no text clipping, and that the preview remains at least120px high. Focus all currently visible choice controls through each narrow tab and require viewport reachability; focusing and viewing must leave saved tables intact. Check native name input identity, draft, selection and focus across four rotations/resizes, with normal native re-focus permitted to reveal it after reflow; Cancel discards it. Existing creator browser cases protect motion, face visibility, reduction and saves. Root will directly inspect every final capture; stills/root-text tests do not certify whole-app zoom, assistive technologies or temporal comfort.
+
+The first fix passed14/15 native checks; at640x360/200% one focused face option extended0.171875px below the viewport. Its artifact and raw failure remain preserved. Scroll margin is a production refinement so the focus outline has room, rather than loosening the viewport assertion. Heavy jobs remain sequential, capped and resource-gated with2GiB reserve.
